---
globs: *.ts,*.json,*.js
alwaysApply: false
---
## Component Structure
* Use OnPush change detection strategy when possible
* Implement OnDestroy for cleanup in components with subscriptions
* Use typed interfaces for component inputs/outputs
* Prefer composition over inheritance

## Import & Module Guidelines
* Use barrel exports for clean imports (index.ts files)
* Group imports: Angular, Third-party, Internal, Relative
* Remove unused imports automatically

## Class Organization
* Order declarations: Decorators → Private Readonly → Private → Public → Constructor → Lifecycles → Getters/Setters → Private Methods → Public Methods
* Private methods and variables should be prefixed with `_`
* Alphabetize declarations
* Use meaningful names that reveal intent

## Method Guidelines
* Methods less than 50 lines where possible
* Use early returns to reduce nesting
* Prefer pure functions when possible
* Methods that could be reused go to services
* App-wide methods go to `app.service.ts`
* Use async/await over .then() chains

## TypeScript Best Practices
* Use early exit strategy
* Avoid nesting
* Use strict TypeScript configuration
* Prefer interfaces over types for object shapes
* Avoid `any` type - use `unknown` or proper typing
* Use utility types when appropriate

## Documentation
* No commenting unless values are "arbitrary" and the source of the values aren't clear
* Use meaningful variable names instead of comments
* Document complex business logic with inline comments

## Translations
* All translations must be added if new values are created. `src/assets/i18n`
* Support all 4 languages when adding new translations
* Use descriptive and hierarchical translation keys
